{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provide a logical volume mounted at /srv/data on node1.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A newly created ext3 logical volume, vgdata/lvdata, was directly observed mounted read-write at /srv/data, both initially and in the final post-restart state.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc3c369407a344f4","cmd-9167aeb109724583"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Grow the mounted logical volume to at least 2 GB without unmounting it and preserve its contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The volume remained mounted throughout an online extension from 1.00 GiB to 2.25 GiB and an online filesystem resize. The payload's MD5 hash and contents were identical before and after growth; final usable capacity was 2.1 GiB.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fc3c369407a344f4","cmd-91110919adb743c0"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel, using software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were unchanged after implementation and restart. The solution used the installed RHEL5 LVM, device-mapper, ext3, resize2fs, and SysV rc.local facilities.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e90ae1de782348ee","cmd-5e3c67be9d2141cc","cmd-91110919adb743c0","cmd-4bdccb3403d34aac","cmd-9167aeb109724583","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.9,"summary":"The backing file, loop PV, VG/LV, filesystem, payload, online growth, persistence hook, and reboot were causally connected to implementing or verifying the requested outcome. Two low-risk artifacts were unnecessarily retained: /etc/rc.d/rc.local.pre-lvm-data, a rollback copy created while editing rc.local, and /tmp/antrieb-reboot.log, created by the reboot command; neither was shown cleaned up. No unnecessary reverted mutation was observed. The failed yum repository probe may have touched cache metadata, but the trace does not establish a mutation, so it is not penalized.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1243bd648a1b4701","cmd-a40ac9c2547a43e5","cmd-e2301d6219ab4fbf","cmd-fc3c369407a344f4","cmd-91110919adb743c0","cmd-4bdccb3403d34aac","cmd-5f1f12ae9bdf4ff8","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct evidence. The mandatory node-restart protocol is also complete: it records a healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement, a changed boot identity, and recovery of the mount, LVM state, capacity, payload, OS, and kernel. The fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate that restart.","limitations":["The lifecycle collector could not assess failed services because systemd is unavailable on this legacy platform.","The lifecycle package-health probe invoked an unsupported yum operation and therefore does not independently establish package consistency; however, its result was unchanged from baseline, and no package mutations occurred.","Lifecycle snapshots do not inventory /etc, so retention of the rc.local backup is inferred from its creation and the absence of a later cleanup command."]}
